  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 306 AM EST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nContinuing into the weekend, the aforementioned surface low is \nexpected to continue moving up the Eastern Seaboard, removing its \ninfluence from the local area and maintaining mostly dry conditions \nthrough the end of the weekend into early next week. The southern \nstream is forecast to shift north across the southern third of the \nCONUS resulting, locally, in mostly zonal flow aloft at the base of \na broad full CONUS trough. Global ensembles are in rather good \nagreement in this evolution through early next week. They begin to \ndiverge a bit around mid-week when the pattern amplifies a bit and a \nshortwave moves across the country bringing our next best chance of \nrain. We should have a stretch of a few generally dry days before\nthen, though. Seasonable temperatures are expected late this \nweekend through early next week.",
